 "claims": [
  "UK: +1pp CPI (and RPI) for three years improves the primary cash need by \u00a33bn a year by 2029 on the leaves' own elasticities (\u00a3-0bn as wired: receipts +\u00a328bn, welfare and departmental spend +\u00a325bn), against \u00a38bn a year of linker uplift accruing to the stock (counted as interest: +0.7pp of revenue). Debt is \u00a323bn higher in 2029; the ratio falls only through the nominal-GDP denominator (-2.2pp of GDP). The flow channel does not rescue the stock argument (linker MTM 2.2% of GDP per +100bp real).",
  "US: the DTS stack indexes $2,050bn of outlays to the COLA and nothing on receipts, so +1pp CPI adds $48bn a year to outlays by 2029 and $25bn a year of TIPS uplift to the stock ($140bn more debt by 2029); the board's revenue is WEO share \u00d7 GDP (unit elasticity by construction, weo_gg), so no receipt leaf is tested.",
  "Euro area: on the shipped bridges +1pp CPI/NGDP improves Germany's primary need by \u20ac-0bn a year by 2029 (revenue \u03b2 1.0, primary spend frozen), Italy's by \u20ac-0bn (tax 0.55 \u00d7 NGDP vs primary 0.35 \u00d7 CPI) and worsens France's by \u20ac0bn (cr\u00e9dits + CAS pensions at \u03b5 1.0 on CPI against receipts whose weighted \u03b5 is below 1); none carries a wage channel. Linker uplift on the board is now tape \u00d7 issuer coefficients (IT/DE/ES/JP); JP has JGBi uplift and no shipped receipt/spend \u03b2."
 ],
 "jp_jgbi_board_patch": {
  "asof": "2026-10-25",
  "method": "board rows for jp under the cpi1_* shocks: uplift = JGBi indexed principal share of marketable stock (ISIN book face x index ratio / snapshot marketable) x board debt path x 1pp in SHOCK_YEARS; written to d_il_accrual_bn / d_uplift_interest_bn, added to d_interest_bn and cumulated into d_debt_bn. The board run left them at 0 because build._marketable caches the baseline components (_COMP) and _uplift returns il_now = 0 outside UK/OFFICIAL, so the shocked accrual never reached the JP book.",
